<title>LEBANON: All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its January 23 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.69 (13.72)	     14.17 (14.21)</p>
<p>    Six months	    14.72 (14.83)	     15.89 (16.01)</p>
<p>    12 months	     14.08 (14.36)	     16.38 (16.76)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 18.12 (18.70)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307  745308</p>
</text>
